ke 'ن' or 'ب', Persian/Urdu letters like پ for ب or ک for ك or گ for ك/ج, visually confused OCR letters like 'ف' vs 'د', or slight vowel variations).\n \n 2. DOSAGE FORM & FORMULATION (ZERO TOL\n<truncated 2927 bytes>\n(\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\") do not change the product.\n-   - \"review\": For the SAME EXACT medicine brand when there is an EXPLICIT, CONFLICTING pack count on BOTH sides (e.g. requested 30 tablets vs candidate explicitly writes 20 tablets of the same medicine).\n+   - \"review\": For the SAME EXACT medicine brand when there is an EXPLICIT, CONFLICTING pack count or bottle volume on BOTH sides:\n+     - Conflicting Tablet/Pack Count: e.g. requested 30 tablets vs candidate explicitly writes 20 tablets of the same medicine.\n+     - Conflicting Bottle/Liquid Volume: e.g. requested 15ml / 15 مل vs candidate explicitly writes 5ml / 5 مل of the same medicine. NEVER silently mark conflicting bottle sizes as \"match\"; mark as \"review\" with reason explaining the volume difference!\n      - Wholesale packaging: If requested specifies retail strips/units (e.g. 2 شريط, 20 قرص) and warehouse specifies wholesale bundles/cartons (باكت / كرتونة / 32ب), mark as \"review\" with the reason explaining the wholesale packaging difference.\n-     - CRITICAL SAFETY: When the trade brand name, form, and strength are identical, NEVER discard as \"no_match\" just because tablet/pack counts differ! It MUST be marked as \"review\" with the reason explaining the packaging difference.\n+     - CRITICAL SAFETY: When the trade brand name, form, and strength are identical, NEVER discard as \"no_match\" just because tablet/pack counts or bottle volumes differ! It MUST be marked as \"review\" with the reason explaining the packaging difference.\n      - Wholesale bundles like \"باكت 120\" (meaning a shipping carton of 120 boxes) or \"باكت 50\" are wholesale lot sizes, NOT the blister/tablet count inside a single box! Do not confuse wholesale carton count with tablet count